## TX 
A lightweight benchmarking CLI for IOTA Move transactions on a local private network, supporting both:
Standard transactions (signed by an EOA / keystore)
Account Abstraction (AA) transactions (signed via MoveAuthenticator and executed under an AA “account address”)
The primary goal is to generate large batches of transactions and correlate them with node-side spans in Tempo/Grafana for execution-time analysis (e.g., spans like handle_transaction, process_certificate).


### Local network + observability setup

Start localnet.
Export required environment variables to enable Tempo tracing:

```bash
export TRACE_FILTER=[handle_transaction]=trace,[process_certificate]=trace
```

Run from the repository root:
```bash
cargo run --release --bin iota start --force-regenesis --with-faucet
```

Start Grafana/Tempo.
Run from tx_bench_framework/metrics:
```bash
docker-compose up -d
```

### Quick start

1. Create abstract account

```bash
cargo run -- --use-faucet init --name <ACC_NAME> --aa-package-path <PACKAGE_PATH> --authenticator <hello-world/ed25519/ed25519-heavy>
```

2. Accounts list 

```bash
cargo run -- accounts list
```

3. Switch active account

```bash
cargo run -- accounts use --name acc1
```

4. Submit transactions

Standard mode: 
```bash
cargo run -- --use-faucet submit --recipient <RECIPIENT_ADDR> --mode standard --count <TX_COUNT>
```

AA mode:
```bash
cargo run -- --use-faucet submit --recipient <RECIPIENT_ADDR> --mode aa --count <TX_COUNT>
```

